      "text": "To solve the system of linear equations\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n3x - 5y = -11, \\\\\n7x + 2y = -12,\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nwe can use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate one of the variables by making the coefficients of \\(y\\) in both equations the same in magnitude but opposite in sign.\n\nStep 1: Multiply the first equation by 2 to align the coefficients of \\(y\\):\n\\[\n2(3x - 5y) = 2(-11) \\implies 6x - 10y = -22.\n\\]\n\nNow our system looks like this:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n6x - 10y = -22, \\\\\n7x + 2y = -12.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Add the two equations to eliminate \\(y\\):\n\\[\n(6x - 10y) + (7x + 2y) = -22 + (-12).\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\\[\n6x + 7x - 10y + 2y = -34 \\implies 13x - 8y = -34.\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\n13x - 8y = -34.\n\\]\n\nFrom this equation, we get:\n\\[\n13x = 8y - 34 \\implies x = \\frac{8y - 34}{13}.\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Substitute this expression for \\(x\\) back into the original first equation to find \\(y\\):\n\\[\n3x - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(x = \\frac{8y - 34}{13}\\):\n\\[\n3\\left(\\frac{8y - 34}{13}\\right) - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left side:\n\\[\n\\frac{24y - 102}{13} - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nMultiply through by 13 to clear the fraction:\n\\[\n24y - 102 - 65y = -143.\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n24y - 65y - 102 = -143 \\implies -41y - 102 = -143.\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\(y\\):\n\\[\n-41y = -41 \\implies y = 1.\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Substitute \\(y = 1\\) back into the expression for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{8(1) - 34}{13} = \\frac{8 - 34}{13} = \\frac{-26}{13} = -2.\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-2, 1)}.\n\\]",
